From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] phy: eusb2: re-apply PHY mode after resume re-initialization

The SM8550 USB2 chain on the AYN Thor is two PHYs: the SNPS eUSB2 high
speed PHY (88e3000, phy-snps-eusb2) chains the PM8550B eUSB2 repeater
via its "phys" property. dwc3 in host mode calls phy_set_mode() once at
probe time (dwc3_core_init_mode) and never again, so the repeater's
host-mode forced-clock workaround (EUSB2_FORCE_EN_5 F_CLK_19P2M_EN /
EUSB2_FORCE_VAL_5 V_CLK_19P2M_EN, written only in eusb2_repeater_set_mode)
is set exactly once per boot.

On s2idle resume dwc3 re-initializes the USB PHY chain through
phy_exit()/phy_init() (full-reinit path, taken because usb@a600000 has
no wakeup-source). phy_exit() on the repeater disables its regulators
and phy_init() re-enables them and rewrites only the tune register
table - the forced-clock bits are lost and never restored, so the USB2
link cannot re-train during port enable. Result after every suspend:

    usb 1-1: reset high-speed USB device ...
    hub failed to enable device, error -108

while the USB3 side survives (the QMP combo PHY re-enables its clocks
via its own runtime-PM resume). Only a physical dock replug recovers
USB2 because it re-initializes the whole electrical path.

Fix: in snps_eusb2_hsphy_init(), re-apply the last known PHY mode to
the repeater after the per-SoC init sequence, mirroring the probe order
(probe runs phy_init() first, then dwc3_core_init_mode() calls
phy_set_mode()). At probe phy->mode is PHY_MODE_INVALID so the call is
a no-op; every resume re-initialization restores the forced-clock bits.

The repeater alone cannot do this: it has no mode tracking - the mode
is stored by the hsphy driver in its phy->mode.

Tested-by: not yet - requires a Thorch kernel rebuild + flash + suspend
cycle verification (3x 10s lid suspend, then 1x ~1h docked).
---
 drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/phy-snps-eusb2.c
@@ -492,6 +492,20 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto disable_clks;
 
+	/*
+	 * dwc3 only calls phy_set_mode() at probe (dwc3_core_init_mode).
+	 * After s2idle the USB PHY chain is re-initialized via
+	 * phy_exit()/phy_init(), but the repeater's host-mode forced-clock
+	 * workaround (EUSB2_FORCE_EN_5 F_CLK_19P2M_EN / EUSB2_FORCE_VAL_5
+	 * V_CLK_19P2M_EN) lives only in eusb2_repeater_set_mode() and is
+	 * never re-applied, so the USB2 link cannot re-train during port
+	 * enable ("hub failed to enable device, error -108"). Re-apply the
+	 * last known mode so the forced clock is restored on every re-init.
+	 * At probe phy->mode is PHY_MODE_INVALID so this is a no-op.
+	 */
+	if (phy->mode != PHY_MODE_INVALID)
+		phy_set_mode_ext(phy->repeater, phy->mode, 0);
+
 	return 0;
 
 disable_clks:
